  "decision_conditions": [
    "Prior to the occupation of the development, full details of hard and soft landscaping shall\rbe submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. All hard and soft\rlandscaping and tree planting shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details\rand to a reasonable standard in accordance with the relevant recommendations of\rappropriate British Standards (in particular, BS 3882: Specifications for Topsoil,\rRecommendations (2015) and BS 8545: Trees from Nursery to Independence in the\rLandscape, Recommendations (2014) or other recognised codes of good practice). The\rworks shall be carried out prior to the occupation of any part or relevant phase of the\rdevelopment or in accordance with the timetable agreed with the Local Planning Authority.\rAny tree(s) or plants that (within a period of five years after planting) are removed, die, or (in\rthe opinion of the Local Planning Authority) are damaged or defective shall be replaced as\rsoon as is reasonably practicable with others of a similar size/species/number as originally\rapproved, unless the Local Planning Authority gives its consent to any variation.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision, establishment and maintenance of a reasonable standard\rof landscape in accordance with the approved designs in accordance with Policy 28 and 30\rof the Sutton Local Plan 2018."
